This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

It is the MUTATION BATTERY behind core/hooks/ai-dlc-derivation-capture.sh. It builds a
throwaway distribution tree, edits COPIES of that hook -- core's own source -- one behaviour
at a time, and re-runs the shipped `derivation-capture` fixture against each mutant to prove
every one of its arms is load-bearing and exclusively so.

`ai-dlc-core-guard.sh` denies a consumer the in-place edit of an installed hook, so the surface
these mutants perturb cannot change in a consumer tree: the assertions are about whether THIS
repository's hook still discriminates, and a consumer that ran them would be re-deriving an
answer about a file it is forbidden to touch.

Its sibling `derivation-capture` SHIPS, and that is the split: the shipped fixture proves the
hook enforces provenance on the consumer's own tree; this one proves the shipped fixture would
notice if it stopped.
